  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Index for a Model of 3d-3d Correspondence for Plumbed 3-Manifolds — We consider the S2 ×q S1 supersymmetric index of a 3d N = 2 theory T[M3] when M3 is a plumbed 3-manifold.\n\n**Index for a Model of 3d-3d Correspondence for Plumbed 3-Manifolds**\n\n*Hee-Joong Chung*\n\n21 pp, 8 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We consider the S2 ×q S1 supersymmetric index of a 3d N = 2 theory T[M3] when M3 is a plumbed 3-manifold. We engineer an eﬀective description of T[M3] from the expression of the homological block for plumbed 3-manifolds as a D2 ×q S1 partition function of a 3d N = 2 theory T[M3] with a boundary condition. We check that the supersymmetric index for such a T[M3] is invariant under the 3d Kirby moves. arXiv:1912.13486v2 [hep-th] 22 Mar 2021\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Supersymmetric index on S2 q S1 and factoriz; 2.1 Supersymmetric index, factorization, and D; 2.2 Analysis on homological block and index of; 3 Supersymmetric index of a 3d N=2 theory on S; 3.1 Engineering a 3d N=2 theory T[M3] from hom; 3.2 Index for an effective description of T[M3",
      "lang": "en",
